<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Gambia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gambia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gambia is a small country in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a> along the Gambia River. The region formed part of the sphere of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaabu-empire">Kaabu Empire</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandinka">Mandinka</a> state that dominated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegambia">Senegambia</a> region for several centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/the-gambia.jpg" alt="The Gambia" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vzb83 iThe source code of the previous SVG was invalid due to 39 errors. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_The_Gambia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…towns such as Sinsani (Sansanding) and Nyamina, bought captives and grain and dealt in Saharan salt, cloth, gold, horses and firearms, and many captives from the middle Niger were sold on to the French and British posts on the Senegal and the <b>Gambia</b> and shipped across the Atlantic.</blockquote><a href="/empire/bamana-empire">Bamana Empire · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>The Kaabu Empire emerged in the thirteenth century as a western province of the Mali Empire, in the region corresponding to present-day Guinea-Bissau, southern Senegal and <b>The Gambia</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kaabu-empire">Kaabu Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The persecution of the Rohingya led <b>The Gambia</b> to bring a genocide case against Myanmar at the International Court of Justice in 2019 and created one of the world's largest refugee camps, at Cox's Bazar in Bangladesh.</blockquote><a href="/empire/myanmar">Myanmar · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>It has also become part of the official national mythology of Mali, the <b>Gambia</b>, Senegal and Guinea, and is studied in history lessons in their primary schools.</blockquote><a href="/songs/epic-of-sundiata">Epic of Sundiata</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1821, after the dissolution of the Company of Merchants, Britain placed its forts on the Gold Coast and its post on the <b>Gambia</b> under the governor of Sierra Leone, Charles MacCarthy, as the British West African Settlements.</blockquote><a href="/state/british-west-africa">British West Africa</a></li><li><blockquote>Duke Jacob Kettler of the Duchy of Courland and Semigallia, who built a merchant fleet, acquired St Andrew's Island in the <b>Gambia</b> River from local rulers in 1651.</blockquote><a href="/state/courland-gambia">Courland Gambia</a></li></ul></section>
